# Project flow context

Before exploring or globbing the repo, **read [`project-flow.md`](project-flow.md)** at the repo root.

- Prefer paths, routes, models, and flows listed there over broad scans.
- Only dig into the codebase when this file lacks what the task needs.
- After meaningful changes to routes, auth, models, hubs, or major flows, **update `project-flow.md`** in the same turn.
- Keep the file limited to codebase project flow (architecture, routes, entities, flows) — no agent instructions, checklists, or changelogs inside it.
- Keep it concise — replace obsolete bullets; do not append forever.
